### Locale Management API Examples
### Use with REST Client extension in VS Code or similar tools

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api
@token = YOUR_AUTH_TOKEN_HERE

### 1. Get all locales (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/locales
Content-Type: application/json

### 2. Get only enabled locales (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/locales?enabled=true
Content-Type: application/json

### 3. Get locale config for frontend (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/locales/config
Content-Type: application/json

### 4. Get single locale (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/locales/en
Content-Type: application/json

### 5. Create new locale - German (protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/locales
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "code": "de",
  "name": "German",
  "nativeName": "Deutsch",
  "isEnabled": true,
  "sortOrder": 4
}

### 6. Create new locale - French (protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/locales
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "code": "fr",
  "name": "French",
  "nativeName": "Français",
  "isEnabled": true,
  "sortOrder": 5
}

### 7. Create new locale - Japanese (protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/locales
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "code": "ja",
  "name": "Japanese",
  "nativeName": "日本語",
  "isEnabled": false,
  "sortOrder": 6
}

### 8. Update locale (protected)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/locales/de
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "German (Updated)",
  "isEnabled": true,
  "sortOrder": 10
}

### 9. Enable/Disable locale (protected)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/locales/ja
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "isEnabled": true
}

### 10. Set locale as default (protected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/locales/en/set-default
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Delete locale (protected)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/locales/ja
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz
Content-Type: application/json
